jobs.description:
Job Summary : Accountable for performing a range of tasks in the administration of thewetland regulations, including planning, monitoring, implementation and evaluation of environmental programs and land use data and issues, and assisting in the development of recommendations for courses of action.

Examples Of Essential Duties

Provides support to the Environmental Protection Commission (EPC) regarding development impacts, regulatory authority and procedures;
Reviews environmental permit applications;
Provides land use information to developers, homeowners and consultants;
Advises on the development of land use plans and regulatory standards;
Advises the Town and others on land use matters relating to environmental protection;
Develops recommendations on wetland permit requests;
Assists in review and analysis of proposed projects for consistency with policies, statutes and environmental impact;
Performs reviews and field inspections to evaluate the impact of development plans pursuant to environmental regulations;
Conducts site investigations;
Assists in drafting new Inland Wetland and Watercourses Regulations to be consistent with State statutes;
Assists in developing and implementing environmental and educational programs;
Assists in developing departmental, regional and local environmental plans and programs;
Assists in formulating policy options;
Assists in preparing environmental impact statements and recommendations for corrective actions and/or alternatives;
Assists in providing technical consultation to local and regional officials and the public;
Assists in research, collection and analysis of resources, data and educational materials;
May introduce expert testimony at public hearings, if appropriate, regarding wetland impacts;
May assist in preparing publications and guidelines on environmental protection, natural resource education and development issues;
May serve as department representative on regulatory and advisory boards and/or committees; and
Performs related duties as required.

Application Deadline : Sunday, October 25, 2026

